Public Stata code accompanying the manuscript:

Persistence in reapplying to university after rejection: Associations with register-based mental health indicators and genetic endowment for educational attainment
Henrik Dobewall, Hannu Lehti, Outi Sirniö, and Maria Vaalavuo

The individual-level Finnish register and genetic data are restricted and cannot be shared by the authors.

## Analyses in the paper

The paper contains two separate analyses:

- **Application outcomes:** person-level analyses in the full analytic sample, distinguishing individuals who never applied, were rejected, or were directly accepted to university. These analyses are cross-sectional and do not use the discrete-time person-year structure.
- **Stop applying after experiencing rejection:** a longitudinal analysis restricted to university applicants whose first application ended in rejection. This analysis uses annual person-years and a logistic discrete-time hazard model.

The public code focuses on the data coding required for the second analysis. Data description presents the data and variables used in both parts of the paper.



## Files

- `00_data_description.md` — data structure, variable definitions, and timing.
- `01_cross_sectional_application_outcomes.do` — person-level descriptive and cross-sectional analyses of application outcomes.
- `02_build_discrete_time_sample.do` — constructs the post-rejection person-year risk set.
- `03_discrete_time_models.do` — estimates the discrete-time hazard models and GxE analyses.

AI assisted the production of this repository. Full code available upon request.
